cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this bench in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Agent Cutoff Bench"
abstract: >-
  Does an agent run a tool call whose arguments were cut off? A model that
  streams a long tool call and stops at its token limit delivers incomplete arguments;
  the safe behaviour is not to run that call. This bench checks what agent frameworks
  actually do, using a fake model server that cuts the same tool call the same way for
  every client. Every per-run record names the client and its version, so each number
  in the write-up can be re-derived instead of trusted.
